WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:05.190 --> 00:00:08.800
We learnt that objects are visible because
of the light getting reflected from

00:00:08.800 --> 00:00:10.830
their surfaces.

00:00:10.830 --> 00:00:15.600
This reflected light enters our eyes and we
see that object.

00:00:15.600 --> 00:00:19.970
What happens inside the human eye when light
rays enter it?

00:00:19.970 --> 00:00:23.250
What is it that
helps us see the things around us?

00:00:23.250 --> 00:00:27.000
The human eye is roughly spherical in shape.

00:00:27.000 --> 00:00:30.560
What we’re going to do in this
video is understand the different parts of

00:00:30.560 --> 00:00:33.810
the eye in short… not in extreme
detail.

00:00:33.810 --> 00:00:35.570
Let’s begin!

00:00:35.570 --> 00:00:38.679
The outer layer of the eye is called the CORNEA.

00:00:38.679 --> 00:00:41.699
It is white in colour and
transparent.

00:00:41.699 --> 00:00:42.699
Transparent?

00:00:42.699 --> 00:00:46.559
Yes, it means that it allows light to pass
through it!

00:00:46.559 --> 00:00:50.359
In fact, cornea REFRACTS or bends the light
passing through it.

00:00:50.359 --> 00:00:53.769
And much of
the refraction inside the eye is done by cornea

00:00:53.769 --> 00:00:55.050
only!

00:00:55.050 --> 00:01:01.620
But wait, it not only refracts light but also
protects the inner parts of the eye.

00:01:01.620 --> 00:01:05.180
It acts like a tough front wall of the eye
protecting the interior of

00:01:05.180 --> 00:01:10.170
the eye from accidents and also does not allow
foreign particles to enter.

00:01:10.170 --> 00:01:13.360
Okay,
so this was all about the outer layer of the

00:01:13.360 --> 00:01:14.360
eye.

00:01:14.360 --> 00:01:18.350
Let’s now talk about the things
present INSIDE.

00:01:18.350 --> 00:01:22.690
Behind the cornea there is a dark muscular
structure called the IRIS.

00:01:22.690 --> 00:01:25.280
Iris
determines the colour of the eye.

00:01:25.280 --> 00:01:29.640
For instance when we say that a person has
blue eyes, it means that the colour of the

00:01:29.640 --> 00:01:32.660
iris of person’s eye is blue.

00:01:32.660 --> 00:01:35.130
Now there
is a small opening at the centre of the iris

00:01:35.130 --> 00:01:36.540
for the light to enter.

00:01:36.540 --> 00:01:38.790
Do you know
what it’s called?

00:01:38.790 --> 00:01:41.460
It is called the PUPIL.

00:01:41.460 --> 00:01:45.250
The Iris actually acts like a shutter of a
camera.

00:01:45.250 --> 00:01:49.550
It controls the amount of light
entering the eye by enlarging or shrinking

00:01:49.550 --> 00:01:51.940
and thereby adjusting the size of the
pupil.

00:01:51.940 --> 00:01:56.310
For example, when you focus the light from
the torch directly into a

00:01:56.310 --> 00:01:59.360
person’s eye the iris shrinks.

00:01:59.360 --> 00:02:01.860
This is because the intensity of light is
too much

00:02:01.860 --> 00:02:03.280
for the eyes to bear!

00:02:03.280 --> 00:02:06.640
The shrinking iris stops the unwanted light
from entering

00:02:06.640 --> 00:02:08.590
through the pupil.

00:02:08.590 --> 00:02:10.720
And when it’s dark or when there’s less
light, it expands

00:02:10.720 --> 00:02:13.570
allowing more light to enter through the pupil.

00:02:13.570 --> 00:02:16.220
Ok, what happens next?

00:02:16.220 --> 00:02:20.569
The light that enters through the pupil falls
on the LENS kept behind.

00:02:20.569 --> 00:02:21.750
This lens
is a BICONVEX LENS.

00:02:21.750 --> 00:02:22.750
What is a convex lens?

00:02:22.750 --> 00:02:24.090
We already know what a biconvex
lens is.

00:02:24.090 --> 00:02:26.970
It is a lens which is thicker at the centre
than the edges.

00:02:26.970 --> 00:02:29.510
It is a CONVERGING
LENS.

00:02:29.510 --> 00:02:33.130
That is, it focuses all the light at one point.

00:02:33.130 --> 00:02:38.450
In a normal regular eye this
point is somewhere here, on this inner boundary

00:02:38.450 --> 00:02:39.450
called RETINA.

00:02:39.450 --> 00:02:42.200
Why do i say a
normal eye?

00:02:42.200 --> 00:02:46.360
Well, in a defective eye, this point of focus
may lie either in front

00:02:46.360 --> 00:02:49.319
of the retina or behind the retina.

00:02:49.319 --> 00:02:54.050
We will talk about this defect of eye in our
future videos but first let’s go back to

00:02:54.050 --> 00:02:58.580
our normal eye where light is focussed
ON the retina.

00:02:58.580 --> 00:03:01.740
Retina is at the back of the eye and marks
the inner layer of the

00:03:01.740 --> 00:03:03.870
eyeball.

00:03:03.870 --> 00:03:06.970
Retina contains lots of NERVE CELLS that sense
the light.

00:03:06.970 --> 00:03:11.010
The nerve cells are of
two kinds namely CONES which are sensitive

00:03:11.010 --> 00:03:15.300
to bright light and RODS which
are sensitive to dim light.

00:03:15.300 --> 00:03:18.990
The message or sensation is then transferred
to the brain along the optic

00:03:18.990 --> 00:03:19.990
nerve.

00:03:19.990 --> 00:03:24.560
Ok, let’s quickly recap what we learned
about human eye.

00:03:24.560 --> 00:03:27.170
Human eye has a roughly spherical shape.

00:03:27.170 --> 00:03:31.620
The outer part of an eye called
CORNEA is a thick white transparent wall,

00:03:31.620 --> 00:03:35.220
which protects the eye from
accidents and keeps the foreign particles

00:03:35.220 --> 00:03:37.770
from entering inside.

00:03:37.770 --> 00:03:40.490
Behind the
cornea, the colourful part of the eye called

00:03:40.490 --> 00:03:42.780
IRIS is present.

00:03:42.780 --> 00:03:46.660
It has a small
opening at the centre called PUPIL.

00:03:46.660 --> 00:03:52.090
Iris controls the light entering through the
pupil by contracting and expanding.

00:03:52.090 --> 00:03:55.790
Behind the pupil there is a converging lens
which focuses the light on retina.

00:03:55.790 --> 00:04:02.050
Retina consists of two types of nerve cells
namely cones and rods.

00:04:02.050 --> 00:04:04.980
They
transfer the message through the optic nerve.

00:04:04.980 --> 00:04:06.970
That’s a lot of information to digest!

00:04:06.970 --> 00:04:13.060
In next video we will talk more about
this lens present inside the eye and will

00:04:13.060 --> 00:04:14.409
discuss its functioning.

